# Source must diff as text.
#
# git decides binary-ness by sniffing for a NUL byte, so one embedded control
# character anywhere in a file makes every change to it render as
# "Bin 6872 -> 8474 bytes" — in review, in blame, in `git log -p`. That is a bad
# outcome for any source file and a genuinely dangerous one for the modules that
# handle credentials, which are exactly where an unreviewable diff should never
# be possible. `connectors/secrets.ts` was in that state, because a NUL is the
# right separator for its AES-GCM additional authenticated data.
#
# `diff` and not `text`: this settles how git RENDERS these files and nothing
# else. `text` would additionally normalize line endings on checkin, which is a
# repo-wide rewrite nobody asked this change to make.
*.ts    diff
*.tsx   diff
*.js    diff
*.mjs   diff
*.json  diff
*.yaml  diff
*.yml   diff
*.md    diff
*.sql   diff
*.css   diff
*.ejs   diff
